---
title: Vegan Black Bean & Walnut Tacos
portions: 6
category: Tacos
source: "https://connoisseurusveg.com/vegan-tacos/"
---

## Filling

[Sweat] Coat the bottom of a large #skillet{} with the @olive-oil{15 ml} and place over medium heat. Add the @onion{110 g}(finely chopped) and sweat, stirring occasionally, until soft and translucent, ~{5 min}.

[Bloom] Stir in the @garlic{6 g}(minced), the @cumin{4 g}, the @chili-powder{2 g}(ancho), the @paprika{2 g}, a pinch of @cayenne-pepper{} and the @walnuts{70 g}(finely chopped). Sauté, stirring constantly, until very fragrant, ~{1 min}.

[Simmer] Stir in the @black-beans{260 g}(drained) and the @canned-tomatoes{120 g}(tomato sauce). Raise the heat and bring to a simmer.

[Braise] Lower the heat and simmer until thick, stirring occasionally. Optionally mash a few beans against the side of the #skillet{} to help thicken the sauce, ~{10 min}.

[Finish] Remove from heat. Stir in the @lime-juice{15 ml} and the @cilantro{5 g}(chopped). Season with @salt{} and @black-pepper{} to taste.

## Serve

[Stuff] Stuff the filling into warmed @corn-tortillas{} and top with shredded cabbage, salsa or guacamole.
